# WebView safe-area CSS injection — do not squash the partner site

The gray-flow shell (`RoostPortal`) injects a CSS override on
`onPageFinished` to neutralise safe-area insets that would otherwise leave
blank strips on notched devices (iPhone Dynamic Island / notch). This
override is easy to overreach with; if it does, the
partner site renders visibly narrower than in a normal mobile browser —
buttons squeezed together and touching the screen edges.

## Symptom

Same URL in the WebView vs. Safari on the same device:

- WebView: content columns extend fully to the left/right edges, no gutters
- Browser: content has natural side padding (~12–24 px) as designed

The site is fine — we broke it with our CSS.

## Root cause

Older template code shipped a rule like this:

```javascript
// ❌ BAD — kills the site's own gutters together with the safe-area gap.
'html,body,#__nuxt,#__layout,#app,#root,' +
'.gameview-mobile-header,.app-header{' +
  'padding-top:0!important;' +
  'padding-left:0!important;' +
  'padding-right:0!important;' +
  'margin-top:0!important;' +
'}';
```

Zeroing `padding-left/right` and `margin-top` on `html/body/#app/#root`
also erases the site's designed horizontal padding — that's what makes the
content look "compressed".

## Correct pattern

Split the injection into two independent responsibilities:

1. **Overwrite the site's own safe-area CSS variables** (`--sat`, `--sab`,
   `--safe-top`, …). Sites that never define such variables are unaffected.
2. **Only touch the visual top spacer**, and only on classes that are
   known sticky/decorative headers — never `html/body/#app/#root`.

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD
var CSS =
  ':root{' +
    '--safe-area-inset-top:0px!important;' +
    '--safe-area-inset-right:0px!important;' +
    '--safe-area-inset-bottom:0px!important;' +
    '--safe-area-inset-left:0px!important;' +
    '--sat:0px!important;--sar:0px!important;' +
    '--sab:0px!important;--sal:0px!important;' +
    '--safe-top:0px!important;--safe-bottom:0px!important;' +
    '--safe-left:0px!important;--safe-right:0px!important;' +
  '}' +
  // Only narrow decorative headers. Never html / body / #app / #root.
  '.gameview-mobile-header,.app-header,.js-safe-top{' +
    'padding-top:0!important;' +
    'margin-top:0!important;' +
  '}' +
  // ✅ LESSON: lock document edges so the page feels native — no rubber-band
  // overscroll that reveals the black scaffold above/below the site.
  'html,body{overscroll-behavior:none!important;' +
    'overscroll-behavior-y:none!important;}';
```

## Separate native-feel injections (keep as their OWN idempotent functions)

These are NOT part of the safe-area patch — ship them as separate injections
on `onPageFinished` (each guarded by its own `window.__flag`):

- **Zoom lock** (`_installZoomLock`): `enableZoom(false)` is NOT enough on iOS.
  Set a viewport meta `maximum-scale=1, minimum-scale=1, user-scalable=no,
  viewport-fit=contain` and `preventDefault` on `gesturestart/gesturechange/
  gestureend` + double-tap. Re-assert on SPA route changes.
- **Tap polish** (`_installTapPolish`): kill the grey box on tap —
  `* { -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent !important; }` and disable the
  long-press callout on non-inputs. Inputs stay selectable.

Both must be re-asserted after a rotation reflow (see
`cold_start_push_viewport.mdc` → `_pokeReflow`).

## Hard rules

- ❌ **Never** apply `padding-left:0!important` / `padding-right:0!important`
     to `html`, `body`, `#__nuxt`, `#__layout`, `#app`, `#root`.
- ❌ **Never** apply `margin-*:0!important` to those elements either.
- ✅ Only touch `padding-top` / `margin-top`, and only on the site's known
     top-spacer class list.
- ✅ Keep the CSS-variable overrides — they only take effect if the site
     already declares those variables.
- ✅ **Skip the whole patch while the keyboard is open** (compositor race —
     on iOS this is a direct cause of keyboard jitter; guard `apply()` with
     `kbOpen()`, see the keyboard-jitter section in `gray_flow_guide.md`).
- ✅ `[FINGERPRINT]` Rewrite the injection body (function/var names,
     sentinel flag, string formatting) per project — identical JS across
     apps is grep-able and clusters the portfolio
     (`gray_part_mixing_review.mdc` §1).

## Verification checklist

Compare side-by-side on a real device before shipping:

- [ ] Open the same partner URL in Safari and in the WebView shell
- [ ] Buttons / cards / grids have identical horizontal gutters
- [ ] No blank strip above the fixed header from safe-area insets
- [ ] Landscape with a notch / Dynamic Island: no white bars on the sides
- [ ] Keyboard open: no reflow / jump when the safe-area timer would fire

If the gutters differ, the injection is over-reaching. Fix the JS payload —
never the native side.
